.TH CLOCK_SETTIME 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
clock_settime \- Linux x86-64 syscall 227
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int clock_settime(int clock, const struct timespec* value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets a clock; privileges may be required.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clock_settime (2)
